{"id": "si-chndm_1921-6-472-6", "status": "ok", "meta": "A flower vase with grotesque ring handles and two nude children at its base, a blackwork print by Paul Birckenhultz, about 1590.", "about": "A vase with grotesque drop-ring handles holds a symmetrical arrangement of flowers. The body of the vase and its base are decorated with strapwork printed in blackwork, and two nude children sit at the foot. Paul Birckenhultz made the print around 1590, and its Latin motto says a docile disposition conquers all difficulties.", "museum_record": "https://collection.cooperhewitt.org/view/objects/asitem/id/35501", "inventory_number": "", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "", "sources": ["https://collection.cooperhewitt.org/view/objects/asitem/id/35501"], "check": "clean"}
