{"id": "si-chndm_1938-88-8668", "status": "ok", "meta": "Mary nurses the Christ child while he twists toward an angel, an engraving of about 1650 by Teresa del Po.", "about": "Mary sits at the right with her eyes downcast and one breast bared, held between her fingers so that the Christ child can feed. He lies nude across her lap, twisting toward an angel at the left of the frame. Tree trunks stand behind them. Teresa del Po made the print around 1650, and the publisher signed it across the bottom.", "museum_record": "https://collection.cooperhewitt.org/view/objects/asitem/id/69758", "inventory_number": "", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "", "sources": ["https://collection.cooperhewitt.org/view/objects/asitem/id/69758"], "check": "clean"}
