{"id": "wd-Q4997694", "status": "ok", "meta": "Emperor Taizong receives the Tibetan envoy in Yan Liben's Palanquin Procession, probably a later copy of the Tang scroll.", "about": "This painting on silk shows a scene of 640, when the Tibetan envoy Gar Tongtsen Yulsung led an embassy to the court of Emperor Taizong of Tang in Chang'an. The scroll is 129 centimeters long and 38.5 wide, and it is in the Palace Museum in Beijing. Wikipedia says it is by Yan Liben, but like other early Chinese paintings the scroll in Beijing is probably a faithful later copy.", "museum_record": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File%3ABuliantu.jpg", "inventory_number": "", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "", "sources": ["https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File%3ABuliantu.jpg", "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4997694", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_Taizong_Receiving_the_Tibetan_Envoy"], "check": "clean"}
